@@ -50,28 +50,39 @@
 
 ### 4. Report
 
-Output a sync report:
+Report format follows `~/.claude/rules/agent-reports.md`. A sync report is one of
+that rule's cross-project exceptions: no character budget, because length scales
+with the number of projects. It is bounded the other way instead — **report only
+what changed.**
+
+A project earns a section only if it has at least one of: a task new since the
+last sync, an overdue task, or an error. Nothing else puts it in the report.
+"No progress note" is **not** a trigger: it is a standing condition across every
+mirror, so triggering on it returns every project every time. It appears as a
+count on a project that already qualified, and nowhere else.
 
 ```
 ## Hermes Sync Report — {YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM}
 
 ### {Project Name} ({PREFIX})
-- Open tasks: N
+- New since last sync: N (list them by local ID and name)
 - Overdue: N (list them by local ID and name)
-- No progress note: N (list them)
-- Last synced: {timestamp from log}
+- No progress note: N (count only, and only on a project already listed above)
 
-[repeat per project]
+[repeat only for projects with a new task, an overdue task, or an error]
 
 ### Errors
-[any from the log, or "None"]
+[any from the log — omit this heading entirely when there are none]
 ```
 
-End with:
+End with this line, whose `Hermes: sync complete` prefix is fixed:
 ```
-Hermes: sync complete — {N} projects updated
+Hermes: sync complete — {N} projects, {N} changed, {N} quiet, {N} errors
 ```
 
+The error count is always present, so "no errors" is distinguishable from "not
+checked". If nothing changed anywhere, that closing line is the whole report.
+
